Proposed (9.2s): Use this skill whenever someone wants to SEE the game — any request for a picture, image, screenshot, PNG, render, sketch, or capture of a scene, level, entity, or moment. Covers: quick flat-colour sketches to eyeball composition or layout; rendered captures of the canvas, with or without HUD; framing one entity alone in a studio shot to judge its model, pose, or silhouette; saving or replaying a simulated moment so the same frame can be re-rendered later; getting an image at a chosen time (e.g. "30 seconds in"), including headless; contact sheets across several steps; naming cameras and views; the pixel size and shape a frame comes out at; producing an image to paste into a doc or share with a person; and getting a rendered frame from a terminal with no tab of your own. Also covers how to ask a vision model about a frame. Prefer engine-data queries first when the question is factual, not visual.

